        "description": "There are different kinds of lies. Some lies only work if the person hearing them might reasonably believe them. They depend on uncertainty, confusion, or missing information. If the lie is exposed, it fails.\n\nBut there\u2019s another kind of lie that works even if everyone knows it\u2019s false. The teller assumes that whether something is true or not just\u2026doesn\u2019t really matter. That\u2019s kind of lie changes how a society works. I don't think you can have a democracy where no one cares about reality. \n\nIf reality doesn't matter...then what does?\u00a0\n\nI'm not going to answer that question for you, but I think you should have an answer.",
